  "notes": [
    "Permutation p-values use the (r+1)/(m+1) convention and can never be exactly zero, which is the honest way to report a test whose null was never matched."
  ],
  "limitations": [
    "Touched elements are inferred from coordinates, not read from the data. A systematic bias in the hit-testing rule, for instance a preference for larger targets, would propagate into this result. The reported hit rate and the clickable-only comparison are the two guards against that.",
    "Elements within a screen are not independent, and one screen can contribute many background elements and one touched element. The permutation test respects the observed marginals but not the nesting; a screen-level cluster bootstrap would be the stronger design and is the natural extension for the journal version."
  ]
